  "plain": "In the 1960s, families for a secret programme were picked partly by demographics, because planners knew a certain share of their children would want to join the military. Dan Sherman, a former Air Force sergeant, says an officer he calls Captain White told him this. If true, it would mean the programme was planned across generations, with children steered into military service."
